---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/PageHero.astro';
import DataControls from '../../components/DataControls.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Data deletion"
  description="Delete your Bundle account and everything stored with it, in one click, with no request to file. Plus the retention rules and your UK GDPR rights."
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Legal"
    title="Delete my data"
    lead="Last updated: 29 September 2026 · One button, immediate, no request to file and nobody to email first."
  />

  <section class="section tight">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <div class="reveal">
        <DataControls heading="h2" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section tight">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <div class="prose reveal">
        <h2>Why it is instant</h2>
        <p>
          Bundle is a static site with no application server behind it. Your
          account, your plan, your holdings and your progress are written to
          your own browser's local storage and have never been transmitted to
          us. There is no database row to find, no backup to purge and no
          processor to instruct, which is why the button above simply does it
          rather than opening a ticket.
        </p>
        <p>
          The one practical consequence worth knowing: because the data lives
          in the browser, deleting it here deletes it <em>here</em>. If you have
          used Bundle on a phone and a laptop, each one holds its own copy and
          each needs clearing.
        </p>

        <h2>What gets deleted</h2>
        <p>
          Everything in the table on the <a href="/legal/cookies">cookie policy</a>:
          your account, investor profile, any unfinished questionnaire,
          recorded holdings, watchlist, Academy progress, newsletter consent
          record and the one-off interface hints.
        </p>
        <p>
          By default your cookie answer and display preferences survive, so
          that deleting your account does not hand you the consent banner again
          as though you had never visited. The confirmation dialog offers to
          clear those too, and clearing your browser's site data for bundle.ai
          removes absolutely everything either way.
        </p>

        <h2>Email and correspondence</h2>
        <p>
          Two things do sit outside your browser, and the button cannot reach
          either.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Newsletter.</strong> If you subscribed, your address is on
            that list. Unsubscribe from any email, or write to
            <a href="mailto:privacy@bundle.ai">privacy@bundle.ai</a>, and it is
            removed rather than suppressed.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Correspondence.</strong> If you have emailed us, that thread
            exists in our mailbox. Ask and we will delete it, unless we are
            required to keep it, in which case we will say which obligation
            applies and for how long.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Retention, in one table</h2>
        <div class="table-wrap">
          <table class="table">
            <thead>
              <tr><th>What</th><th>Where it lives</th><th>Kept for</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td>Account, plan, holdings, progress</td>
                <td>Your browser</td>
                <td>Until you delete it, here or in browser settings</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Newsletter subscription</td>
                <td>Our mailing list</td>
                <td>Until you unsubscribe or ask for removal</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Consent records (cookies, newsletter)</td>
                <td>Your browser, and the list for newsletter consent</td>
                <td>Kept while the consent stands, as evidence that it was given</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Email correspondence</td>
                <td>Our mailbox</td>
                <td>Up to two years after a thread closes, or sooner on request</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <h2>Your rights under UK GDPR</h2>
        <p>
          You have the right to be told what we hold, to get a copy, to have it
          corrected, to have it erased, to have it in a portable format, and to
          restrict or object to certain processing. The two buttons above are
          the copy right and the erasure right, exercised directly. For anything
          else, one email to
          <a href="mailto:privacy@bundle.ai">privacy@bundle.ai</a> is enough; no
          form, no identity-verification hoop unless we genuinely cannot tell
          who is asking.
        </p>
        <p>
          We aim to answer well inside the one-month statutory deadline. You can
          also complain to the Information Commissioner's Office
          (<a href="https://ico.org.uk" rel="noopener">ico.org.uk</a>), though we
          would rather have the chance to put it right first.
        </p>

        <h2>If Bundle ever holds data on a server</h2>
        <p>
          Accounts are local today because there is nothing yet that needs a
          server. If that changes, this page changes with it, before the feature
          ships, not after: what is stored, where, for how long, and how to get
          it deleted. The commitment that will not change is that erasure stays
          a button rather than becoming a process.
        </p>

        <h2>Related</h2>
        <p>
          <a href="/legal/privacy">Privacy policy</a> ·
          <a href="/legal/cookies">Cookie policy</a> ·
          <a href="/legal/terms">Terms of use</a> ·
          <a href="/legal/refunds">Refund policy</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
